# Details page wizard edit

Related: [details-page-cards.mdc](details-page-cards.mdc) (inline page-level Edit), [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc), [feature-page-layout.mdc](feature-page-layout.mdc), [core-hosted-peer-dialog](../skills/core-hosted-peer-dialog/SKILL.md), [form-creation](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md), [item-list](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md).

Use when the entity’s create/edit flow is a **multi-step wizard** (catalog services, company registration, Identity profile, and similar). Do **not** use for showcase/simple demos that keep **inline** page-level Edit — those stay on [details-page-cards.mdc](details-page-cards.mdc).

Self-edit-only wizards (no list Add) are allowed when there is no create list — e.g. Identity profile: edit-only dialog with `initialStep` from section cards.

## Flow

```text
List Add / Edit  ──┐
                   ├──► same *FormDialog wizard (id? + initialStep?)
Detail card Edit ──┘         create: no id, step 1
                             edit:   id set, step = card map
```

## Required composition

```text
FeaturePage
  onBack (icon before title); actions: extra CTAs only (no page-level Edit / Cancel / Save)
  Outer: grid items-start gap-6 lg:grid-cols-3
    Left:  flex flex-col gap-6 lg:col-span-2
    Right: flex flex-col gap-6 lg:col-span-1
      Editable sections → EditableSectionCard (hover Edit3 → openWizard(step))
      Meta / audit → plain Card (no edit)
```

| Piece | Requirement |
|-------|-------------|
| Shell | `FeaturePage` — full width; same 3-col grid as details-page-cards |
| Back | Always `onBack` + `backLabel` — ghost icon-only `ArrowLeft` immediately before the title → parent list |
| Overview gallery | When the entity (or linked catalog items) has images → `ImageCarousel` first in left stack (see below) |
| Cards | View-only content; no inline fields on the details page |
| Per-card Edit | `EditableSectionCard` with `canEdit` + `onEdit` → `openWizard(n)` |
| Meta cards | Plain `Card` — timestamps / references stay non-editable |
| Dialog | **One** shared wizard for list Add/Edit and detail section Edit (or edit-only when there is no create list) |
| Mode | `isNew = !id` when create is supported — no separate `mode` prop; self-edit may omit `id` |
| Step jump | `initialStep` (standalone) / `?step=` on embed path |

## Overview ImageCarousel (mandatory when gallery images exist)

Keep Overview UI aligned across catalog, company catalog, and linked entities (e.g. events). When gallery images are available, render `@webonone/ui-kit` **`ImageCarousel`** as the **first** card in the **left** column — before section cards.

```tsx
{overviewGalleryImages.length > 0 ? (
  <Card>
    <CardContent className="pt-6">
      <ImageCarousel images={overviewGalleryImages} alt={entityDisplayName} />
    </CardContent>
  </Card>
) : null}
```

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Props | `images: { mediaId: string; url: string }[]`, `alt` = entity / service display name |
| Placement | Left stack (`lg:col-span-2`), **above** Basics / Service / etc. |
| Empty | **Omit** the Card when `images.length === 0` — do not ship an empty carousel shell |
| Wrapper | Plain `Card` + `CardContent className="pt-6"` — **not** `EditableSectionCard` |
| Source | Entity `galleryImages` / `displayGalleryImages`, or combined linked galleries (events: service + space, dedupe by `mediaId`) |
| Gallery tab | Optional separate Gallery tab for manage/edit; Overview still shows the carousel |

Forbidden: Overview missing the carousel when images exist; using `ImagePreview` for multi-image Overview galleries; inventing a custom carousel.

## Section tabs URL sync

When a details or settings page has a **section tablist** (Overview / Gallery / Sessions / etc.), sync the active tab with the query param **`?tab=<id>`**. Do not keep the tab in local `useState` only.

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Query key | `tab` |
| Default | Omit `tab` from the URL when the default tab is selected |
| Invalid / missing | Fall back to the page default |
| History | `setSearchParams(..., { replace: false })` so Back/Forward restores the tab |
| Paths | Do **not** use path segments for section tabs on an entity route that is already `…/:id` |
| Wizard steps | Keep embed/wizard entry on `?step=N` — do **not** overload `tab` for wizard steps |

Prefer a small service-local helper (e.g. `useDetailTabParam(allowed, defaultTab)`) so allowed tabs can shrink per kind/role (stale `?tab=variants` on a non-product falls back to default).

Applies to wizard-backed details **and** settings pages with the same tablist pattern (Basic Settings, Email settings).

Forbidden: local-only tab state when a section tablist is shown.

## Dual-use wizard (mandatory when create exists)

List **Add** and detail/list **Edit** must share the same `*FormDialog`:

| Opener | Props |
|--------|-------|
| List Add | `open`, no `id`, `initialStep` default `1` |
| List Edit | `open`, `id`, step `1` |
| Detail card | `open`, `id` (when applicable), `initialStep` = section → step map |
| Self-edit only | `open`, `initialStep` — e.g. Identity profile |

**Every wizard body** must show centered `Step {n} of {total} — {StepTitle}` above the progress bar — see [dialog-windows.mdc](dialog-windows.mdc) § Wizard dialogs. Do not ship a bar alone.

Embed routes: `/embed/dialogs/<kind>/create` and `/embed/dialogs/<kind>/:id/edit` (or `/embed/dialogs/profile/edit`) with optional `?step=N`. Hosted chrome: [core-hosted-peer-dialog](../skills/core-hosted-peer-dialog/SKILL.md).

On save from the details page: refresh detail when needed and close the dialog.

## EditableSectionCard

Copy the Data `EditableSectionCard` shape per feature (not in UI Kit yet). **Do not invent different Edit chrome.**

| Requirement | Exact chrome |
|-------------|--------------|
| Placement | Top-right of `CardHeader`, beside title/description (`flex items-start justify-between gap-3`) |
| Visibility | Hover-reveal on the card (`Card className="group"`) |
| Control | Outline **icon-only** `Button` — `variant="outline"` `size="icon"` — **no** visible “Edit” text label |
| Icon | Lucide `Edit3` with `className="h-4 w-4"` `aria-hidden` |
| Classes | `shrink-0 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100` |
| A11y | `aria-label={`Edit ${title}`}` |
| Gate | Render only when `canEdit && onEdit` |

```tsx
<Card className="group">
  <CardHeader>
    <div className="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
      <div className="min-w-0 flex-1 space-y-1.5">
        <CardTitle className="text-lg">{title}</CardTitle>
        {description ? <CardDescription>{description}</CardDescription> : null}
      </div>
      {canEdit && onEdit ? (
        <Button
          type="button"
          variant="outline"
          size="icon"
          className="shrink-0 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100"
          onClick={onEdit}
          aria-label={`Edit ${title}`}
        >
          <Edit3 className="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden />
        </Button>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="space-y-4">{children}</CardContent>
</Card>
```

Forbidden Edit chrome: `size="sm"` with text “Edit”, always-visible labeled buttons, page-level Edit in `FeaturePage` actions.

## Forbidden (this pattern)

- Page-level Edit / Cancel / Save on the details page
- Separate create-only vs edit-only dialogs for the same entity
- Section-only save APIs (wizard still submits the full entity)
- Local `CustomDialog` inside `#main-content` when embedded — use peer-dialog
- Using this pattern for showcase/simple **inline** page-level Edit ([details-page-cards.mdc](details-page-cards.mdc))
- Per-card Edit that does not match the hover icon chrome above
- Section tablist with local-only tab state (must sync `?tab=`)
- Overview without `ImageCarousel` when gallery images exist (or a one-off image UI instead of UI Kit)

